WEBVTT

00:04.820 --> 00:06.190
The Abyss.

00:06.650 --> 00:11.660
It's formed when the concentration of mana
in the atmosphere reaches critical mass.

00:12.620 --> 00:15.620
The Abyss links this world and
the demon world, Void.

00:15.620 --> 00:20.460
The deeper the connection is, the more
powerful beasts will be manifested.

00:25.840 --> 00:30.510
That night, the abyssal depth
in my hometown was 12.

00:32.680 --> 00:36.140
A depth that is able to manifest
a beast called Lord.

00:37.850 --> 00:41.150
I never thought that
I would swing this again.

00:43.230 --> 00:44.520
Grandpa.

00:45.400 --> 00:48.240
Noel, we have to get out of here now.

00:57.240 --> 01:00.460
Listen, Noel.
Don't leave this place.

01:00.460 --> 01:02.960
You will be safe inside this shelter.

01:03.580 --> 01:04.960
What about you?

01:04.960 --> 01:08.210
I'll hold them off until
help from the Empire arrives.

01:08.210 --> 01:08.960
Liar!

01:08.960 --> 01:11.590
There's no way to tell
when help will arrive.

01:11.590 --> 01:13.340
I know you're going to fight them alone.

01:14.800 --> 01:17.350
It's impossible.
If you do that, you will—

01:17.350 --> 01:18.560
Don't look down on me.

01:21.310 --> 01:23.560
Have you forgotten who I am?

01:23.560 --> 01:27.940
I'm the man who's called Overdeath.

01:28.570 --> 01:30.240
Don't worry.

01:30.240 --> 01:35.120
Your grandpa is gonna protect you
with his life.

01:36.530 --> 01:37.740
Grandpa!

01:38.080 --> 01:39.790
Grandpa!

01:45.790 --> 01:49.920
Noel, men can't let anyone
look down on them.

01:49.920 --> 01:53.300
No matter when, no matter what.

02:10.360 --> 02:12.150
Grandpa...

02:25.120 --> 02:26.710
Grandpa.

02:27.250 --> 02:28.670
Grandpa!

02:32.590 --> 02:34.010
Grandpa!

02:38.010 --> 02:40.720
I guess, I can't beat age, huh.

02:40.720 --> 02:43.730
To think Overdeath would
end up like this...

02:44.690 --> 02:47.690
This is the fate of Seekers.

02:48.400 --> 02:55.200
Choosing a life of combat means that the
god of death will always be by your side.

02:56.070 --> 03:01.160
Noel, even knowing this,
do you still want to be a Seeker?

03:01.910 --> 03:05.870
Will you travel the same path
as this old man?

03:12.050 --> 03:15.800
Yes, I'm gonna be a Seeker.

03:17.550 --> 03:21.600
Then you must become
the strongest Seeker.

03:21.600 --> 03:24.270
Can you promise me?

03:24.270 --> 03:26.230
I promise.

03:26.230 --> 03:29.270
I will become the strongest Seeker.

03:31.230 --> 03:37.200
As expected of my grandson.

03:38.410 --> 03:46.870
Noel... I'll always love you.

03:50.210 --> 03:53.710
My grandpa's name is Brandon Stollen.

03:53.710 --> 03:56.970
He was the strongest Seeker
who once defeated

03:56.970 --> 04:00.800
the beast with an abyssal depth of 13,
Cocytus the Silverfish,

04:00.800 --> 04:04.180
and then he gained
the nickname Overdeath.

04:05.680 --> 04:07.350
It's been two years since then.

04:10.400 --> 04:14.610
As promised, I became a Seeker.

04:15.570 --> 04:18.070
Llyod and Walter, attack!

04:19.570 --> 04:20.950
Tanya, back them up!

04:20.950 --> 04:21.870
Got it!

04:26.410 --> 04:27.620
Eat this!

04:29.500 --> 04:33.040
Talker, the weakest support class.

04:33.380 --> 04:35.380
That's my job.

04:58.193 --> 05:03.520
I have belief raised in my heart,
invisible to the eye

05:03.520 --> 05:07.660
It becomes a weapon that pierces through
the uncontrollable darkness

05:07.660 --> 05:13.125
Because I don't want to lose

05:13.130 --> 05:17.710
I just need to get stronger

05:17.710 --> 05:20.250
The story has begun to move

05:20.250 --> 05:22.867
I have a choice to make

05:22.870 --> 05:28.356
I've discarded my hesitation
since long ago

05:28.360 --> 05:30.976
To surpass the abyss

05:30.980 --> 05:33.479
I'm falling into the dark

05:33.480 --> 05:39.255
Beyond the sorrow

05:39.260 --> 05:44.240
I will definitely reach it

05:44.240 --> 05:51.160
A world no one knows

05:51.160 --> 05:57.489
Turning everything into strength

05:57.490 --> 06:00.360
And I will seize it

06:00.360 --> 06:03.876
The tactics to win

06:06.930 --> 06:08.930
Lesser Vampire.

06:08.930 --> 06:12.640
They're the lower-class of vampire-types
that cannot use magic.

06:12.640 --> 06:17.560
Instead, their main body, the queen,
is able to reproduce in a short time.

06:17.560 --> 06:20.440
Giving birth to an unlimited
amount of spawns.

06:21.400 --> 06:26.410
Does that mean they're all
the offspring of the main body?

06:26.410 --> 06:28.740
That's right.
But don't let your guard down.

06:29.200 --> 06:33.370
Each one of the spawns has
the strength to tear apart an ox.

06:37.380 --> 06:40.670
And it won't die
unless its head is cut off.

06:40.670 --> 06:42.670
Isn't that right, Noel?

06:43.670 --> 06:44.590
Yeah.

06:47.470 --> 06:49.350
Hey, Noel.

06:49.350 --> 06:51.310
If there's the main body,

06:51.310 --> 06:56.060
then we should go straight to kill it,
rather than killing its spawns like this.

06:56.690 --> 07:00.270
If we kill the main body,
the spawns should stop moving.

07:00.270 --> 07:01.940
It would be the most efficient way—

07:01.940 --> 07:02.990
We can't.

07:02.990 --> 07:03.780
Huh?

07:03.780 --> 07:08.740
Actually, this mission is difficult
for a C-rank like us.

07:08.740 --> 07:12.580
If we're able to sweep the spawns
before dealing with the main body,

07:12.580 --> 07:14.910
our success rate would be higher.

07:14.910 --> 07:17.000
Don't weigh everything by its efficiency.

07:17.620 --> 07:18.960
Or you'll die.

07:19.790 --> 07:22.250
Yes, yes. Roger that.

07:22.250 --> 07:26.010
Since you, the buffer of our party,
have the right to give us the orders.

07:26.010 --> 07:29.050
That's how Blue Beyond works.

07:29.050 --> 07:30.300
Hey, Walter!

07:31.760 --> 07:35.640
We, the C-rank Seekers,
can take this B-rank mission

07:35.640 --> 07:40.110
thanks to the skills and directions
of the Great Talker Noel.

07:41.060 --> 07:44.030
Talker is a job specialized in support.

07:44.780 --> 07:50.120
A Talker can enhance the party's
combat power with buff words,

07:50.990 --> 07:54.410
but the fighting ability is the weakest.

07:54.950 --> 07:57.920
I can only fight by relying on comrades.

07:58.580 --> 08:02.250
That's the reason why this job
is ridiculed as the weakest.

08:03.750 --> 08:06.510
Walter, let me say this to you.

08:07.090 --> 08:08.010
Everyone, get down!

08:10.800 --> 08:12.300
What's this smell?

08:12.300 --> 08:13.680
Is it poisonous gas?

08:13.680 --> 08:15.640
Noel is in danger.

08:15.640 --> 08:17.810
We have to rescue him first.

08:17.810 --> 08:19.560
Tanya, make sure to follow us.

08:19.560 --> 08:21.150
Got it!

08:22.150 --> 08:23.110
Tanya!

08:32.280 --> 08:34.950
Damn it, I can't hit as hard
as I usually do.

08:35.290 --> 08:40.290
Without Noel's buffs,
we've got no chance of winning.

08:40.290 --> 08:42.380
Give us your orders, Noel!

08:42.720 --> 08:44.500
Say something!

08:44.500 --> 08:47.510
You're supposed to be the Talker!

08:49.800 --> 08:52.180
Don't look down on me!

08:55.720 --> 08:59.230
Don't you dare look down on me!

08:59.810 --> 09:01.270
Noel!

09:01.270 --> 09:07.110
I'll show you how a Talker fights.

09:07.110 --> 09:12.360
Talker Skill: Tactician!

09:15.280 --> 09:17.370
By giving orders to the party,

09:17.370 --> 09:21.460
it'll increase the abilities of
the members by 25%.

09:21.460 --> 09:23.040
A ranged attack is coming!

09:23.040 --> 09:24.460
Both of you, fall back!

09:27.840 --> 09:30.800
Battle Voice!

09:31.260 --> 09:35.140
It increases the recovery speed of party
members' stamina and mana by 25%.

09:35.850 --> 09:38.060
Tanya, cast a barrier for them!

09:38.060 --> 09:39.060
Got it!

09:39.060 --> 09:41.310
Lloyd and Walter, resume the attack!

09:41.310 --> 09:42.270
- Understood!
- Leave it to me!

09:48.070 --> 09:49.030
Noel!

09:50.240 --> 09:51.990
Some spawns were hiding?

09:51.990 --> 09:53.070
Not good.

09:53.070 --> 09:55.570
If they join the fight...

09:55.570 --> 09:58.370
Peer Support!

09:58.370 --> 10:02.460
It stabilizes the target's mental state
and reinforces their willpower.

10:02.460 --> 10:04.040
Seventy-four seconds.

10:04.420 --> 10:06.250
I'll take care of the small fry!

10:06.250 --> 10:08.130
Three of you, focus on the main body!

10:08.420 --> 10:10.590
Tanya, keep the barrier up!

10:11.010 --> 10:13.800
Lloyd and Walter,
keep dodging and attacking!

10:13.800 --> 10:16.640
Prepare your strongest attack!

10:18.560 --> 10:20.270
Stop!

10:20.560 --> 10:23.480
Stun Howl!

10:25.560 --> 10:28.440
Magic gun Silver Flame.

10:28.440 --> 10:32.320
The only anti-beast weapon that
a Talker like me can rely on.

10:32.940 --> 10:34.820
Ice Bullet!

10:40.990 --> 10:42.750
One got away.

10:42.750 --> 10:44.870
One bullet left.

10:44.870 --> 10:48.210
Out of a total of 74 seconds,
43 seconds remaining.

10:48.210 --> 10:51.710
It'll reach me in 23 seconds.

10:51.710 --> 10:53.670
It's according to my calculations.

10:55.880 --> 10:59.510
Assault Command.

10:59.850 --> 11:01.520
Now, do it! Lloyd! Walter!

11:01.520 --> 11:04.520
Use your attack skills on the main body!

11:04.520 --> 11:06.230
Aura Blade!

11:06.230 --> 11:08.150
Deadly Drive!

11:12.820 --> 11:13.900
We did it!

11:13.900 --> 11:15.200
We did it, Noel—

11:20.620 --> 11:22.830
If we kill the main body,

11:24.290 --> 11:27.040
the spawns will stop moving.

11:30.000 --> 11:32.210
Precisely 74 seconds.

11:32.210 --> 11:34.880
No threatening presence,
confirmed.

11:34.880 --> 11:37.180
The battle is over.

11:37.720 --> 11:39.430
Good work, everyone.

11:39.430 --> 11:41.810
Blue Beyond, mission complete.

11:42.760 --> 11:47.350
Although the movement of the spawns
will stop after the main body is defeated...

11:47.350 --> 11:49.100
You were too reckless.

11:49.100 --> 11:50.360
Stupid.

11:54.740 --> 11:56.070
Don't cry, Noel!

11:56.070 --> 11:59.450
But they said I got the weakest job.

11:59.450 --> 12:03.450
I want to be a Warrior like you, Grandpa.

12:04.120 --> 12:09.000
Noel, you look exactly like
your deceased mother.

12:09.000 --> 12:10.880
But I know.

12:11.380 --> 12:17.010
You have a talent as a Seeker
that she didn't have.

12:17.010 --> 12:19.430
Who cares if you're a Talker or whatever?

12:19.430 --> 12:22.850
I'm gonna raise you to be
the strongest Seeker.

12:23.510 --> 12:25.430
Trust me.

12:28.190 --> 12:29.730
I believe you.

12:29.730 --> 12:32.060
I'll become a Seeker like you.

12:32.060 --> 12:37.490
No, I'll become the strongest Seeker
who surpasses the Overdeath,

12:37.490 --> 12:41.450
even if I'm a Talker, the weakest job.

12:41.990 --> 12:44.993
(Why the Weakest Aims to
Become the Strongest)

12:45.950 --> 12:48.790
Etrai, the capital of the Velnant Empire.

12:49.410 --> 12:53.960
The prosperity of this capital is
due to the civilization of magic.

12:53.960 --> 12:57.420
This empire is more susceptible to
the Abyss than most countries.

12:57.880 --> 13:02.100
The Velnant Empire developed
magical technology

13:02.100 --> 13:04.680
using materials derived from
research on beasts.

13:05.430 --> 13:09.480
You can say that it's the main
pillar of the country.

13:10.140 --> 13:12.480
Therefore, the Seeker who cleansed
the city from the Abyss

13:12.480 --> 13:16.780
and hunted down the beasts,
becomes a figure admired by the people.

13:17.730 --> 13:19.320
Cheers!

13:19.320 --> 13:23.030
Once I became 15 years old
and was able to become a Seeker,

13:23.030 --> 13:26.700
I decided to search for companions
in Etrai.

13:26.700 --> 13:30.580
Talkers are the weakest.
They can't fight alone.

13:30.580 --> 13:33.380
All things considered, we did great.

13:33.380 --> 13:36.000
After all, we earned five million fil.

13:36.000 --> 13:37.460
Walter, the Warrior.

13:37.460 --> 13:40.050
We've come so far, haven't we?

13:40.050 --> 13:41.720
Tanya, the Healer.

13:41.720 --> 13:43.680
It's been a year since
we formed this party.

13:43.680 --> 13:47.220
We can probably aim higher.

13:47.220 --> 13:49.470
Llyod, the Swordsman, and our leader.

13:49.770 --> 13:52.100
You could say it's a pretty decent party.

13:52.100 --> 13:54.440
It would be better if we had a Scout.

13:54.810 --> 13:57.940
But for now, I need to gather
experience with them.

13:57.940 --> 14:00.490
That's the first step to my ambition.

14:00.490 --> 14:02.650
What's wrong?

14:02.950 --> 14:05.240
This is a celebration, you know?

14:05.240 --> 14:07.740
But you don't look happy.

14:07.740 --> 14:08.870
It's nothing.

14:08.870 --> 14:10.870
Don't be like that!

14:10.870 --> 14:13.420
You've got worries?
Talk to me!

14:13.420 --> 14:14.330
Leave me alone.

14:14.330 --> 14:18.090
Don't tell me you're still mad
about the reward.

14:18.090 --> 14:21.300
That we refused to negotiate for
another five hundred thousand?

14:21.720 --> 14:24.180
It's not good to be so hung up on money.

14:24.180 --> 14:26.890
A Seeker must be big-hearted.

14:26.890 --> 14:31.390
Your grandpa would have said
the same thing as well.

14:32.230 --> 14:33.270
Listen.

14:33.270 --> 14:36.100
Seekers must obsess over money.

14:36.100 --> 14:41.530
You have to bring the best items
and equipment for exploration.

14:41.860 --> 14:45.240
You can't do anything and can't reach
a higher position without money.

14:45.240 --> 14:47.660
No need to care about what
other people say.

14:47.660 --> 14:51.790
Being labeled evil
is a medal for a Seeker.

14:51.790 --> 14:54.160
Just look at me, I've been called
Overdeath the Undying Demon.

14:54.540 --> 14:55.870
Just remember this.

14:55.870 --> 14:58.170
Don't let anyone look down on you.

15:00.750 --> 15:04.340
I'm not mad or anything,
this matter has already been settled.

15:04.340 --> 15:07.640
He's right. Isn't you the one
who keeps bringing that up?

15:07.640 --> 15:09.050
You're so pathetic.

15:09.600 --> 15:11.600
Which one is more pathetic?

15:11.600 --> 15:16.730
Noel, if you're so stingy about money,
it'll affect Blue Beyond's reputation.

15:16.730 --> 15:17.980
Reflect on your actions!

15:17.980 --> 15:20.940
Yes, yes, I'm wrong.

15:20.940 --> 15:23.070
Everything's my fault.

15:23.070 --> 15:27.280
The Great Walter is never wrong,
after all.

15:27.280 --> 15:29.240
Watch your tone!

15:29.240 --> 15:31.700
I'm two years older than you!

15:31.700 --> 15:34.960
What's the relation of our age with this?

15:34.960 --> 15:36.410
Don't make me laugh.

15:36.410 --> 15:38.790
Ability is everything for a Seeker.

15:38.790 --> 15:45.300
Using your age as a shield to force others
to agree with you is pretty naive, Walter.

15:45.300 --> 15:46.550
Don't mess with me!

15:46.550 --> 15:49.550
Don't get carried away when you can
only issue orders from the back!

15:49.550 --> 15:54.060
The people who hide in a safe place
while we bet our lives taking the aggro

15:54.060 --> 15:56.350
have no right to be cocky!

15:57.850 --> 16:00.810
So that's your real feeling, huh?

16:01.690 --> 16:03.820
It's only natural.

16:03.820 --> 16:09.950
Compared to incompetent me,
the Great Walter fights like a raging devil.

16:09.950 --> 16:11.660
You truly are a Seeker among Seekers—

16:13.080 --> 16:14.580
I'll kill you.

16:14.580 --> 16:18.040
Bring it on.
I'll accept your challenge.

16:18.040 --> 16:20.000
That's enough.

16:20.000 --> 16:23.630
Doing it here is what you call pathetic.

16:24.590 --> 16:27.470
Both of you are really idiots.

16:27.470 --> 16:28.800
Don't say that.

16:28.800 --> 16:31.680
Both of them are our precious comrades.

16:31.680 --> 16:35.390
It's about time to call it a day.
Let's split the reward.

16:39.600 --> 16:41.810
Just this much?

16:41.810 --> 16:47.690
Party operational costs, equipment
repairs, and payment to the clan.

16:47.690 --> 16:51.820
After many expenses,
each person only received 250,000 fil.

16:51.820 --> 16:54.030
Even though that mission
was so difficult.

16:54.370 --> 16:58.160
But our party's funds are
steadily increasing.

16:58.160 --> 17:02.960
When we take on another big mission,
we'll make this much again.

17:02.960 --> 17:04.130
Tsk.

17:04.130 --> 17:08.720
Llyod, missions like this are rare.

17:08.720 --> 17:14.140
Unlike clans, we don't get missions
directly from the country.

17:14.140 --> 17:15.720
Well, you're right.

17:16.140 --> 17:21.560
Almost all Abyss purification tasks
are handled by clans.

17:21.560 --> 17:26.730
If we fail, we have to pay the penalty.

17:28.440 --> 17:31.650
Anyway, how much does our party
have saved away?

17:32.410 --> 17:37.290
Let's see, including this,
we have a total of 12.8 million fil.

17:37.290 --> 17:41.370
Then let's use that money
to establish a clan.

17:44.380 --> 17:47.919
Noel, in order to establish a clan,

17:47.920 --> 17:50.800
we have to pay
20 million fil to the country.

17:50.800 --> 17:52.380
I know it very well.

17:52.970 --> 17:56.550
That's why, I'll provide
the remaining 7.2 million fil.

17:56.550 --> 18:02.520
Rather than doing secondhand jobs,
it's better if we establish a clan.

18:02.520 --> 18:08.070
To establish a clan, we need to have
a base of operations in the capital.

18:08.070 --> 18:09.360
Think about the high rent.

18:09.360 --> 18:11.360
I already have a lead on a cheap place.

18:11.360 --> 18:13.910
But we're still newbies.

18:13.910 --> 18:17.620
We're still C-rank.
There's no way we could pull it off.

18:17.620 --> 18:19.790
Then, when will we be ready?

18:19.790 --> 18:24.540
Can you tell me in how many years
we will be able to pull it off?

18:25.000 --> 18:30.800
If we don't run a clan,
we'll always be newbies.

18:30.800 --> 18:32.050
That's...

18:32.050 --> 18:33.970
While working as a Seeker,

18:33.970 --> 18:36.550
I've been studying about clans
all the time.

18:36.550 --> 18:39.060
I have all of the necessary knowledge.

18:39.060 --> 18:43.940
What's left is the experience we get
by actually running a clan.

18:44.390 --> 18:47.940
That's not something that we can
acquire if we stay at a standstill.

18:48.730 --> 18:51.900
But we're still young.
We have no experience.

18:51.900 --> 18:56.570
If we don't have the country's trust,
we won't get big payment jobs—

18:56.570 --> 18:58.530
It's the opposite, Lloyd.

18:59.160 --> 19:02.120
We'll get it because
we're young and good-looking.

19:02.120 --> 19:04.040
That's the most important thing.

19:04.040 --> 19:06.580
The country wants more Seekers.

19:06.580 --> 19:10.840
In other words, they want more of
their people to become Seekers.

19:10.840 --> 19:15.260
A great Seeker is considered
both an idol and a hero.

19:15.260 --> 19:18.180
They have to be young,
attractive, and strong.

19:18.180 --> 19:23.020
All the successful clans are filled
by those types of people.

19:23.020 --> 19:28.400
And if you sign a contract with a company,
you also get a sponsorship fee.

19:28.400 --> 19:29.560
Let me get this straight.

19:29.560 --> 19:34.990
The country is going to treat us better
because we're good-looking?

19:34.990 --> 19:38.570
Yeah. And you're included, Walter.

19:38.570 --> 19:41.780
You have many flaws indeed,
but you have one strong point.

19:41.780 --> 19:42.370
Huh?

19:42.370 --> 19:46.040
Isn't it like
we're trying to sell ourselves?

19:46.040 --> 19:47.830
I'm in.

19:47.830 --> 19:50.340
I've gotten tired of doing
secondhand jobs.

19:50.340 --> 19:52.590
Let's make a clan as soon as possible.

19:52.590 --> 19:53.960
Walter!

19:53.960 --> 19:56.130
I'm serious, Tanya.

19:56.130 --> 20:00.550
Status, fame, and money.
Nothing wrong with wanting that.

20:00.550 --> 20:02.970
I can even sleep with as many
good women as I like.

20:03.310 --> 20:05.100
Or, what?

20:05.100 --> 20:09.100
Will you be my woman instead?

20:10.060 --> 20:11.400
Walter!

20:13.230 --> 20:15.490
It's two to one.

20:15.490 --> 20:18.700
Llyod, tell us your opinion as the leader.

20:19.490 --> 20:23.160
You really want to establish a clan now,
no matter what?

20:23.450 --> 20:25.660
For this alone,
I've no intention of compromising.

20:25.660 --> 20:29.370
If you say no, then hand over
my share of our savings.

20:29.750 --> 20:32.790
I'll quit the party.

20:33.290 --> 20:35.760
I believe I told you this
when we formed this party.

20:35.760 --> 20:37.840
I have a dream.

20:37.840 --> 20:42.720
To become the greatest Seeker,
more than the legendary Overdeath.

20:43.680 --> 20:45.680
Dream, huh...

20:49.310 --> 20:52.440
Fine, let's establish a clan.

20:52.440 --> 20:54.190
Lloyd, are you serious?

20:54.570 --> 20:58.570
We're going to arrive at this point
sooner or later anyway.

20:58.570 --> 21:02.620
Noel, I've told you my opinion
as the leader.

21:02.620 --> 21:03.950
Are you satisfied?

21:03.950 --> 21:05.830
Yeah, no more complaints.

21:05.830 --> 21:09.910
How about we continue this tomorrow—
No, at lunch the day after tomorrow?

21:09.910 --> 21:13.670
Let's talk after we rest and get
the alcohol out of our bodies.

21:13.670 --> 21:16.210
Got it. The day after tomorrow.

21:16.210 --> 21:20.010
I'm glad that you understand.
Llyod, Tanya.

21:20.550 --> 21:21.380
See you later.

21:22.340 --> 21:23.590
Noel!

21:29.230 --> 21:30.770
Have a good rest.

21:32.100 --> 21:33.440
You too.

21:45.200 --> 21:46.780
We've got a problem, Noel!

21:47.790 --> 21:49.950
Calm down and listen!

21:49.950 --> 21:52.620
Llyod and Tanya...

21:52.960 --> 21:55.420
They betrayed us!

22:17.482 --> 22:23.760
Will you understand my word?

22:23.760 --> 22:29.990
Do you hear my voice telling you?

22:29.990 --> 22:36.276
Will you join to fight with me?

22:36.280 --> 22:42.380
Do you get what it means?

22:42.380 --> 22:47.950
Cause I see all crystal clear
among all tangled strings

22:47.950 --> 22:54.596
I need to treat it as cold as
threads with cold blood

22:54.600 --> 23:00.550
Instead of taking sugarcoated pills
to make you eased

23:00.550 --> 23:07.532
I directly talk inside your head
to make you strong

23:09.707 --> 23:12.890
Cause I see it

23:12.890 --> 23:15.975
We can break

23:15.980 --> 23:19.160
The old empire

23:19.160 --> 23:22.270
With our powers

23:22.270 --> 23:25.300
Make it over

23:25.300 --> 23:28.387
In near future

23:28.390 --> 23:32.557
With no fear

23:34.976 --> 23:39.981
(The Talker Shows No Mercy)
